  "notes": "The collective preset, and its one hard-sourced harmonic fact is a strange and useful one: the documented device is a stock-library world-music loop used raw — \"Praise the Lord\" is built on a GarageBand panpipe sample with no chord movement under it. So the melodic layer is a single modal woodwind figure: `monophonicBias` 0.95, `intervals` weighted heavily to steps, `timbreHint` `bright_pluck`, and the harmony below it is nothing but the 808 holding tonic and 5th. That is why `bass808.slideIntervals` is exactly P5 and P8 and why `chordDurationBeats` reaches 32 beats. The posse-cut structure is the other authored thing: `verse` is 8–16 bars because members hand off with no re-intro, `hook` is 4 bars because the research says the hook is a 4-bar chant, `outro` is 8–12 because the ad-lib outros are long, and `dropOutBeats` is 0.85 because the beat drops to the loop at every handoff. `snare.reverb` is `short` — the heavy short-plate on the clap reading as the room is a stated trait. ⚠ `medium` is the research's own rating, and it marks the drum and 808 specifics `[LOW-CONF]`: those two blocks are the inferred parameters here, read off the collective's records rather than off any statement. ⚠ `minor_pentatonic` in the scale bank is INFERRED — the research says only \"minor, single-mode, drone-based\" plus an Andean panpipe source; pentatonic is the honest reading of that source, not a documented claim. ⚠ The `i–VII` family is INFERRED. The research names static i only; it carries the lowest weight and exists because the generated chord part still owes a producer 55 distinct outputs over 200 seeds. ⚠ **The countermelody reached only 979 distinct answers in 1000 seeds against a floor of 980**, so it was given range: densityRatio 0.45. A counter is combinatorial in the styles it may pick, its density against the melody, and the phrase length it answers inside — one style over a thin density inside a single phrase length has almost nothing a seed can vary.",
